Use full local_raw_evidence and preceding_source_index. Find the actual nearest main-text predecessor; hints and ownership proposals are fallible. Do not skip an intervening genuine main paragraph, invent missing characters, or use a following page as a predecessor.

A word can be split at a page edge. In alphabetic scripts this can be a prefix and suffix, with normal line-end hyphenation. In Chinese and other unspaced scripts a single lexical expression can also span the edge. Require an actual contiguous word completion at the immediate seam, not merely related meanings or the possibility of placing two complete words next to each other.

Judge the literal word seam before any subsequent punctuation or parenthetical author/editor comments. A comment after the completed word does not undo that word completion. This does not approve the comment's semantics or change its ownership.

